 for chemical workers exposed to 2,3,7,8-tetrachlorodibenzo-<italic>p</italic>-dioxin</article-title><source>Occup Environ Med</source><year>2003</year><volume>60</volume><issue>9</issue><fpage>672</fpage><lpage>675</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12937189</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib8"><label>8.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Collins</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Bodner</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilken</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Serum concentrations of chlorinated dibenzo-<italic>p</italic>-dioxins and dibenzofurans among former Michigan trichlorophenol and pentachlorophenol workers</article-title><source>J Expo Sci Environ Epidemiol</source><year>2007</year><volume>17</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>541</fpage><lpage>548</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17426737</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib9"><label>9.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Aylward</surname><given-names>LL</given-names></name><name><surname>Bodner</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Collins</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Exposure reconstruction for a dioxin-exposed cohort: integration of serum sampling data and work histories</article-title><source>Organohalogen Compd</source><year>2007</year><volume>69</volume><fpage>2063</fpage><lpage>2066</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><label>10.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ott</surname><given-names>MG</given-names></name><name><surname>Olsen</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Cook</surname><given-names>RR</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Cohort mort